{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"SessionStart:startup","toolUseID":"96c805cb-6a98-4548-9291-199d7200c5ea","hookEvent":"SessionStart","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"SessionStart\",\"additionalContext\":\"## User profile (global-memory/USER.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 1,375 chars. Updated when the agent learns durable user preferences. -->\\n# User Profile\\n\\n## About\\nEric Rash, Director of Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Builds football GPS and force-plate pipelines. Wife Kristina; kids Ames, Saylor, Rowan (5, 4, 10mo on 2026-09-01). Career target: analytics-first player-coach near Iowa, $90K+ floor, mid-2027. Read `~/DEV/ContextVault` before career or personal advice.\\n\\n## Preferences\\n- Python/R. Two machines: Windows by day, Mac by evening (split 9/24). Tool paths: machine.md.\\n- Local SQLite/DuckDB. No cloud servers or schedulers without Baylor IT approval. Google Drive only; keep DuckDB local to avoid sync locks.\\n- Tangible working examples over documentation.\\n- Staff-facing text: Athletic Performance (not S&C), Athletic Medicine (not sports medicine), Applied Performance (not sport science).\\n\\n## Working Style\\n- Direct; says \\\"stop\\\" when done. Challenge vague or rehearsed reasoning: \\\"sharpened, not soothed.\\\"\\n- Decide standard technical details, state the choice, and move on.\\n- Build in small steps. Do not break mid-season work.\\n- Authors direction when leadership does not; OKR-driven change agent in a status-quo group.\\n- Right question over downstream craft; Christian faith is his organizing frame.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Working memory (global-memory/MEMORY.md)\\n\\n<!-- Cap: 2,500 chars. Working scratchpad; writes take effect next session. -->\\n# Working Memory\\n\\n## Active Threads (max 5; park one to add one)\\n- **Status report**: biweekly to 12/18. →Tier A supervisor-log-pipeline\\n- **SW/Tech Review (10/1)**: Erin asked; NEXT Teams 10/2, ET by 11/30. →`SoftwareTech_Review/docs/`\\n- **Ship queue (9/25)**: q2wk to a named user: RI5 #002 wk 9/28, intern M1 10/9, AP Digest ch1 10/23. →`RunningTheRoom/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- **PP Recruiting (9/30)**: 017 sent-ready; 018 SHIP. NEXT send 018, walkthrough. →`PP_Recruiting/docs/`\\n- **RTP CLA (9/26)**: L1–2 built. NEXT Tim/Jacob export; Joe → L3. →`RTP_Constraints_Course/docs/`\\n\\n## Parked (NEXT lives in each STATUS.md; `where-was-i.py` lists them)\\n- Slate CLEARED 10/3; registry 171 rows, 7-day rule, /landed; NEXT design PM system →`project-triage/docs/STATUS.md`\\n- Personal site: scroll-craft LOCAL, Artifact live →Tier A personal-site-build-routes\\n- FB matchups: W5 ASU done, W1-4 backfilled; `pff_game_result.py`; bye wk = mid-season →`MatchupAnalysis_FB2026`\\n- Flint: Supertraining Ch1-7 in vault (10/3); NEXT Ch8 on Mac →`Flint`\\n- 42Analytics: NEXT captions (429s) on Mac →`42Analytics`\\n- VB GRID: fix merged 10/2 (#2); await Mike's reply →`Volleyball_GRID`\\n- Sleep sched: NEXT night/early-kickoff →`sleep-scheduler`\\n- TypeSafe: MAINTENANCE; PR #31 merged as record →`TypeSafe_Sandbox`\\n\\n## Environment Notes\\n- Machine split (9/24): Win=day, Mac=eve; Mac sole writer GPS/Perch/VALD.\\n- Hooks: patch both copies for shared events. →Tier A hook-two-copies-trap.\\n- daily-backup: manifest entries alone copy nothing; sweep nested ~/.claude repos →handoff 09-19.\\n- `DEV/Linda Projects` = private I-983 repo; folder has a space, repo an underscore.\\n- `~/DEV` = THIN repo; `.gitignore` starts `/*` — never remove. →Tier A github-consolidation.\\n- Win: Drive sync, junction and renv traps →machine.md. PFF: swap Parquet on Drive, never the DB; `PFF_DB`.\\n- Schedules →automation-cadence. CFB capture Mac only. Dashboard →command-centre.\\n- Post-merge: delete merged branches unasked (verify) →Tier A post-merge-cleanup.\\n- Sessions: start `where-was-i.py`, prune with `session-sweep.py` →Tier A session-hygiene.\\n\\n## Pending Decisions\\n- None open. (OKR gate + OKRs_2026-27 CLOSED 10/2: Eric not developing further.)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## HOOK FAILURES — surface these to the user on the first response\\n\\n- **daily-backup** ×1 (2026-10-03 23:53 → 2026-10-03 23:53 UTC): 1 error(s): repo-behind-blocked:global-memory - see ~/.claude/scripts/logs/daily-backup.log\\n- **adjudicate-budget-tripped** ×1 (2026-10-04 13:00 → 2026-10-04 13:00 UTC): stopped after 335,350 / 250,000 tokens\\n\\nFull log: `~/.claude/global-memory/transcripts/.errors.log`. Surface this once; clear the file after the user has seen it and the cause is handled.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Cross-harness activity (KeystoneOS unified snapshot)\\n\\nNot loaded here — read it only if a question needs it.\\nPath: `/Users/kristinarash/DEV/KeystoneOS/outputs/dashboard/unified-snapshot.md` (4905 chars, updated 2026-10-04 12:17)\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"Loading unified cross-harness snapshot...","durationMs":632},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e1f9fe43-7073-4016-8c2e-ad9a4657c41d","timestamp":"2026-10-04T13:05:23.096Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-py","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/global-memory","sessionId":"d865cfb7-24d5-4992-b93f-b18ac6fe3e3f","version":"2.1.259","gitBranch":"main"}
